// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Marauder_Marauder 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2243799435" "Praetor White, as he is known on Praetoria, heads up the Powers Division for Emperor Cole. These super-powered individuals act as the ultimate police force in keeping Praetoria the utopia it appears to be. All the while Praetor White feeds on the instability of the government and makes his own opportunities to look good."
// GroupDescription :
// DisplayNames :
"P472388814" "Marauder"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Marauder_Minion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1254617691" "Marauder recruits only the most hungry and violent men into his ranks. He trains them hard enough to either turn them into rock or kill them. Those that graduate from this regimen are disciplined and deadly."
// DisplayNames :
"P2061193977" "Rampager"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Marauder_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3572740050" "Marauder is extremely adept at spotting leadership potential and tactical aptitude. When he sees these qualities in one of his men he gives them the chance to lead small groups and operations as a test. There is only one price for failure."
// DisplayNames :
"P2813767534" "Wrecker"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Marauder_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2578295751" "If a Wrecker shows a high success rate, Marauder gives them one final test: pick a Destroyer and defeat him in single combat. The fight is to the death. If the Wrecker wins, he has a new title and greater responsibilities. This test is typical of the Darwinian approach that Marauder is committed to."
// DisplayNames :
"P2914641356" "Destroyer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Marauder_Nictus_Hunter_Minion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2431954468" "Rampager Quantum"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Marauder_Nictus_Hunter_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1964502969" "Wrecker Quantum"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Marauder_Nictus_Hunter_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3336736523" "Destroyer Quantum"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Marauder_P_Marauder 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Marauder_P_Marauder_Artillery_Barrage 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P643012170" "Artillery Barrage"

